{
  "dom_id": "step-q84192",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Find the smallest natural number solution to the system of linear congruences below.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x≡2 & (\\text{mod}\\,3) \\\\ x≡4 & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\ x≡5 & (\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $3,$ $7,$ and $8$ are coprime, then according to the Chinese remainder theorem, the system has a unique solution modulo $3\\cdot 7\\cdot 8=168.$\n\nWe will solve the system in two steps.\n\n**Step 1.** Find the common solution for the first and second congruences of the system.\n\nFrom the first congruence, we get\n\n$$\nx≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\,⟹\\,x=2+3t,\\,t\\in Z.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second congruence, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡4 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\ 2+3t & ≡4 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\ 3t & ≡2 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $7$ is a relatively small modulus, we can solve it by trial and error. We have that $5\\cdot 3≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).$ So, we multiply both sides by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3t & ≡2 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\ 5\\cdot 3t & ≡10 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\ t & ≡3 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $t=3+7s,$ where $s\\in Z.$ Substituting this into the expression for $x,$ we get the common solution for the first and second congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2+3t \\\\  & =2+3(3+7s) \\\\  & =11+21s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2.** Find the common solution of all three congruences.\n\nNow, substituting the common solution of the first two congruences into the third congruence, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡5 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 11+21s & ≡5 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 21s & ≡-6 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 5s & ≡2 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $8$ is a relatively small modulus, by trial and error, we have that $5\\cdot 5≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).$ So, we multiply both sides by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5s & ≡2 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 5\\cdot 5s & ≡10 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ s & ≡2 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $s=2+8u,$ where $u\\in Z.$ Substituting this into the expression for the common solution of the first two congruences, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =11+21s \\\\  & =11+21(2+8u) \\\\  & =53+168u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x≡53\\,(\\text{mod}\\,168)$ is the unique solution modulo $168,$ and $x=53$ is the smallest natural number solution to the system.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
